WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:02.940
The market is full of data,

2
00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:04.560
and the research could go on forever.

3
00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:06.580
So where do you start?

4
00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:09.340
This is the method,

5
00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:11.020
and it has four stages.

6
00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:16.620
Stage one is to define our goal and our objectives.

7
00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:21.740
Stage two is to analyse the competitors' online activity.

8
00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:27.620
Stage three is to characterise the market,
the competition and the demand.

9
00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:31.820
And stage four is to formulate the strategy,

10
00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:35.260
and the optimal course of action
to reach those objectives.

11
00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:40.060
Now, a word about managing expectations.

12
00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:42.940
Do not expect to analyse all of the data,

13
00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:44.840
or to understand every meaning in it.

14
00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:47.980
This field carries very large quantities of information.

15
00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:49.860
It takes a lot of experience,

16
00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:52.020
and it involves a lot of tedious work.

17
00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:55.140
So when a decision is large enough to justify it,

18
00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:57.760
have a professional market research conducted.

19
00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:02.020
Next, you will build an example plan,

20
00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:03.400
one column at a time.

